{"tool_name":"rearrvisr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"rearrvisr","home":"https://github.com/dorolin/rearrvisr","summary":"The R package rearrvisr provides functions to identify and visualize inter- and intrachromosomal translocations and inversions between a focal genome and an ancestral genome reconstruction, or two extant genomes. Rearrangements, breakpoints, and synteny blocks are identified along the focal genome and output in a tabular format. Rearrangements and synteny blocks can be visualized along the focal genome by two graphical functions.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:35:19Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-04T15:32:20Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:rearrvisr","credit":[{"email":"doro.lindtke@gmail.com","name":"Dorothea Lindtke","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Ancestral reconstruction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3745"},{"term":"Genome visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3208"}]}],"name":"rearrvisr","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.06.25.170522"}],"topic":[{"term":"Evolutionary biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3299"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Paleogenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3943"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"rearrvisr","home":"https://bio.tools/rearrvisr","summary":"The R package rearrvisr provides functions to identify and visualize inter- and intrachromosomal translocations and inversions between a focal genome and an ancestral genome reconstruction, or two extant genomes. Rearrangements, breakpoints, and synteny blocks are identified along the focal genome and output in a tabular format. Rearrangements and synteny blocks can be visualized along the focal genome by two graphical functions.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{